{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EtfY7x9c3H31gA4tYfoh4n","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tset: Fenwray Film Society\n3\trole: governing\n4\tcovers: \"Behaviour at society activities, complaints and member suspensions\"\n5\t---\n6\t# Conduct and Complaints\n7\tFenwray Film Society is a fictional organisation.\n8\t\n9\tAdopted: 18 March 2025\n10\tEffective: 1 April 2025\n11\t\n12\t## 1. Expected behaviour\n13\t1.1 Members and visitors must treat others respectfully.\n14\t1.2 Threats, harassment and deliberate disruption are prohibited.\n15\t1.3 Visitors must follow reasonable instructions from duty volunteers.\n16\t1.4 Recording a screening without permission is prohibited.\n17\t1.5 Smoking and vaping are not permitted in the hired room.\n18\t\n19\t## 2. Immediate action\n20\t2.1 A duty volunteer may ask someone to stop disruptive behaviour.\n21\t2.2 A person who refuses may be required to leave the activity.\n22\t2.3 Serious threats may result in immediate removal without a warning.\n23\t2.4 The duty volunteer must record the incident within 48 hours.\n24\t2.5 Immediate removal does not itself end society membership.\n25\t\n26\t## 3. Complaints\n27\t3.1 Complaints may be submitted in writing to the secretary.\n28\t3.2 The secretary acknowledges a complaint within five working days.\n29\t3.3 A person named in a complaint must be allowed to respond.\n30\t3.4 The committee normally decides a complaint within 21 calendar days.\n31\t3.5 A committee member directly involved must not vote on that complaint.\n32\t\n33\t## 4. Suspension\n34\t4.1 The committee may suspend membership for up to 30 calendar days.\n35\t4.2 A suspension requires a majority vote of uninvolved committee members.\n36\t4.3 The written decision must state the reason and suspension dates.\n37\t4.4 Membership rights during suspension are governed by film-membership.md.\n38\t4.5 The member may request one review within seven calendar days.\n39\t4.6 The committee decides a review within 14 calendar days.\n40\t\n41\t## 5. Records and refunds\n42\t5.1 Complaint records are kept for 24 months after closure.\n43\t5.2 Access is restricted to the secretary and uninvolved committee members.\n44\t5.3 Removal from an event does not automatically create a refund right.\n45\t5.4 Refund eligibility is determined by film-refunds.md.\n46\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"cb43a242-8fa5-407f-8c04-f0566d298008","uuid":"97e87e87-d1e8-4f4f-ab4a-f74c14801bd4","timestamp":"2026-10-12T17:16:42.179Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\tc\\3VJB\\reference\\film\\film-conduct.md","content":"---\nset: Fenwray Film Society\nrole: governing\ncovers: \"Behaviour at society activities, complaints and member suspensions\"\n---\n# Conduct and Complaints\nFenwray Film Society is a fictional organisation.\n\nAdopted: 18 March 2025\nEffective: 1 April 2025\n\n## 1. Expected behaviour\n1.1 Members and visitors must treat others respectfully.\n1.2 Threats, harassment and deliberate disruption are prohibited.\n1.3 Visitors must follow reasonable instructions from duty volunteers.\n1.4 Recording a screening without permission is prohibited.\n1.5 Smoking and vaping are not permitted in the hired room.\n\n## 2. Immediate action\n2.1 A duty volunteer may ask someone to stop disruptive behaviour.\n2.2 A person who refuses may be required to leave the activity.\n2.3 Serious threats may result in immediate removal without a warning.\n2.4 The duty volunteer must record the incident within 48 hours.\n2.5 Immediate removal does not itself end society membership.\n\n## 3. Complaints\n3.1 Complaints may be submitted in writing to the secretary.\n3.2 The secretary acknowledges a complaint within five working days.\n3.3 A person named in a complaint must be allowed to respond.\n3.4 The committee normally decides a complaint within 21 calendar days.\n3.5 A committee member directly involved must not vote on that complaint.\n\n## 4. Suspension\n4.1 The committee may suspend membership for up to 30 calendar days.\n4.2 A suspension requires a majority vote of uninvolved committee members.\n4.3 The written decision must state the reason and suspension dates.\n4.4 Membership rights during suspension are governed by film-membership.md.\n4.5 The member may request one review within seven calendar days.\n4.6 The committee decides a review within 14 calendar days.\n\n## 5. Records and refunds\n5.1 Complaint records are kept for 24 months after closure.\n5.2 Access is restricted to the secretary and uninvolved committee members.\n5.3 Removal from an event does not automatically create a refund right.\n5.4 Refund eligibility is determined by film-refunds.md.\n","numLines":46,"startLine":1,"totalLines":46}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01EtfY7x9c3H31gA4tYfoh4n","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
